Task: Set up Vitest for unit testing in both Main and Renderer processes

Summary:
Established comprehensive testing infrastructure for the Electron application, with separate configurations optimized for Node.js (Main/Preload) and browser (Renderer) environments.

Files Created:
- vitest.config.ts - Vitest configuration for Main and Preload processes (Node.js environment)
- vitest.renderer.config.ts - Vitest configuration for Renderer process (jsdom environment)
- src/renderer/test/setup.ts - Global test setup for Renderer tests with jest-dom matchers and IPC mocking

Files Modified:
- package.json - Added comprehensive test scripts for different testing scenarios
- package-lock.json - Added Vitest, @testing-library/react, @testing-library/jest-dom, jsdom dependencies

Technical Decisions:
1. Separate Vitest configs for different process types due to environment differences
2. Used jsdom for Renderer tests to simulate browser environment
3. Configured global test setup to automatically mock window.ipcRenderer
4. Enabled globals in Vitest for cleaner test syntax (describe, it, expect available without imports)
5. Added coverage reporting with v8 provider for >80% coverage target
6. Created flexible npm scripts for various testing workflows (watch mode, UI mode, coverage)

Test Commands Created:
- npm test: Runs all tests sequentially (main then renderer)
- npm run test:main: Main/Preload tests only
- npm run test:renderer: Renderer tests only
- npm run test:main:watch: Watch mode for Main/Preload
- npm run test:renderer:watch: Watch mode for Renderer
- npm run test:ui: Launch Vitest UI for interactive testing
- npm run test:coverage: Generate coverage reports

Verification:
- npm run test:main: ✓ Config valid, ready for tests
- npm run test:renderer: ✓ Config valid, ready for tests
- Both configurations successfully parse and run

Rationale:
Provides the testing foundation required for TDD workflow. Separate configurations ensure optimal test environment for each Electron process type, with appropriate mocking and setup for each context.
